WEBVTT

NOTE Synthetic transcript for evals. Company, people and figures are invented.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:14.000
<v Aida Bekova>Thanks for joining. Today we walk through the draft requirements from your BRD.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:32.000
<v Sara Lind>On cancellations: we discussed it internally. Two hours is too strict. Members should be able to cancel up to 1 hour before the class.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:40.000
<v Omar Haddad>Fine from IT, the rule is the same effort either way.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:50.000
<v Aida Bekova>So the cancellation window becomes 1 hour instead of 2. Agreed?

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:53.000
<v Sara Lind>Agreed.

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:22.000
<v Aida Bekova>The waitlist: when a class is full, members join a waitlist and move in automatically when a place frees up. Is that right?

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:30.000
<v Sara Lind>Yes, that's exactly right. Confirmed.

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:58.000
<v Sara Lind>One addition: when a place frees up, the member on the waitlist must accept it within 30 minutes, otherwise it goes to the next person.

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:06.000
<v Omar Haddad>We can do that.

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:30.000
<v Sara Lind>And trainer ratings, let's drop them. Nobody asked for it and trainers don't want it.

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:35.000
<v Aida Bekova>Understood, ratings are out.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:07:02.000
<v Omar Haddad>Just an idea: QR check-in at the club door could measure no-shows exactly.

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:12.000
<v Sara Lind>Interesting, but not now. Let's not go there yet.

00:07:40.000 --> 00:08:02.000
<v Omar Haddad>One risk from IT: ClubDesk's API has a request limit. At peak hours the booking sync could lag, and members would see places that are already gone.

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:10.000
<v Sara Lind>That would hurt. Omar, can you look into it?

00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:14.000
<v Omar Haddad>Yes, I'll own that.

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:28.000
<v Sara Lind>The reminder 24 hours before the class stays as it is.

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:35.000
<v Aida Bekova>Great. Thanks everyone.
